 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Do you have fast internet connection? It might be that if it' slow, the image is buffering heavily. Shoot in a room with a big open window, so the light is good, and keep the window as the background. Shoot in front of the window with the camera off it. Shoot with few objects between you and the window, like opening the door. Use the microphone your computer hears well, like the one on your earphones. Keep it straight on, about eye level. Shoot in room where you want to be, and try to look at the window.",
